---
description: C# access modifier conventions for Unity scripts
globs: Assets/Scripts/**/*.cs
alwaysApply: false
---

# Explicit Access Modifiers

Always write access modifiers explicitly. Do not rely on C# defaults.

## Fields

```csharp
// BAD — implicit private
[SerializeField] Camera _camera;
Plane _groundPlane;

// GOOD
[SerializeField] private Camera _camera;
private Plane _groundPlane;
private const int MaxEnergy = 3;
```

## Methods

```csharp
// BAD — implicit private
void Update() { }
void HandleTouch() { }

// GOOD
private void Update() { }
private void HandleTouch() { }
```

## Public surface

Only expose what other classes need:

```csharp
public class GameManager : MonoBehaviour
{
    public static GameManager Instance { get; private set; }

    public void StartBusiness() { }

    private void Awake() { }
    private void InitSystems() { }
}
```

## Unity lifecycle

Unity invokes private lifecycle methods via reflection — keep them private:

```csharp
private void Awake() { }
private void OnEnable() { }
private void Update() { }
private void OnValidate() { }
private void OnDrawGizmosSelected() { }
```

## Plain C# classes

Same rule applies to domain/system classes under `Assets/Scripts/`:

```csharp
public sealed class Customer
{
    public CustomerState State { get; private set; }

    private float _eatTimer;

    public void Tick(float deltaTime) { }
    private void TransitionTo(CustomerState next) { }
}
```
